Relax CUDA test tolerances for rotated bounding-box transformations.

The affine bounding-box tolerance change is a backport of upstream commit:
https://github.com/pytorch/vision/commit/ca2212438fdd8ce29b66999ed70ed54b0f9372d1

With PyTorch 2.9.1 and CUDA 12.9.1, torchvision 0.24.1 shows small
CPU-vs-CUDA numerical differences for rotated float32 XYWHR bounding boxes
in resize and crop tests. Relax the tolerances only for these CUDA cases.

Ensure the CUDA JPEG device test uses an RGB image. The test selects the
first non-CMYK JPEG returned by a recursive glob, which may be a grayscale
image depending on file ordering. CUDA JPEG encoding only supports
three-channel images, so explicitly decode the test image as RGB.

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT5.6
